  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe strategy employs an adaptive heuristic search combining global exploration with local refinement to escape local minima. The core idea is to use multiple optimization passes with increasing resolution, starting from a low-resolution approximation and progressively refining it. Each pass uses Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) for global exploration, followed by Sequential Quadratic Programming (SLSQP) for local refinement. The resolution is doubled iteratively, allowing the solution to capture finer details while maintaining feasibility.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nThe problem is to find h: [0,2] \u2192 [0,1] with \u222bh(x)dx=1 that minimizes:\nC\u2085 = max_k [\u222bh(x)(1 - h(x+k))dx] \nThe optimization uses:\n- Variables: h[i] \u2208 [0,1] for i = 0,...,n_points-1\n- Objective: Minimize max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, 'full')) * dx\n- Constraints: sum(h) * dx = 1\nThe PSO-SLSQP pipeline balances global exploration and local convergence.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Start with n_points=70, doubling to 140 and 280 if time permits.\nb. For each resolution:\n   i. Initialize PSO swarm with particles based on lower-resolution solution.\n   ii. Run PSO to explore global minima, tracking best candidate.\n   iii. Use best PSO solution as initial guess for SLSQP refine.\n   iv. Validate and store best feasible solution.\nc. Each PSO particle maintains feasibility through projection:\n   - Clip values to [0,1]\n   - Scale to ensure sum(h)=n_points/2\nd. SLSQP uses mod='SLSQP', bounds=[0,1], constraint sum(h)=n_points/2\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- PSO hyperparameters: swarm size=30, maxiter=100, inertia=0.7, c1=1.5, c2=1.5\n- Initial guess: interpolated lower-resolution solution\n- Resolution schedule: [70, 140, 280] with adaptive stopping\n- Swap to SLSQP after PSO to leverage quadratic convergence\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Time allocation: 3min/PSO pass + 2min/SLSQP pass per resolution\n- Robustness features:\n  - Feasibility projection for PSO particles\n  - Adaptive step size in SLSQP\n  - Early stopping on confidence intervals\n  - Best solution retention\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Final solution must satisfy:\n  - 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 \u2200i\n  - sum(h) = n_points/2\n  - C\u2085 evaluated accurately via correlate()\n- Final check ensures numerical stability and feasibility",
